================================================================================
Regarding AutoIt and AutoItX
================================================================================

AutoIt and AutoItX are products of AutoIt Consulting Ltd.

This project is NOT affiliated with, endorsed by, or sponsored by AutoIt
Consulting Ltd. The name "autoitx" is used descriptively, to identify the API
this library is compatible with.

The AutoItX3 DLL is NOT distributed with this crate, is NOT a dependency in the
Cargo sense, and no part of it is vendored into this source tree.

On Windows, this library loads `AutoItX3_x64.dll` at runtime from a location you
provide. You must obtain that DLL yourself, from the official AutoIt
distribution at https://www.autoitscript.com/, and your use of it is governed by
AutoIt's own licence terms — not by this project's licence. AutoIt is freeware
distributed under a EULA; note in particular that commercial use requires
acknowledging AutoIt in your product and linking to the AutoIt homepage.

See docs/windows-setup.md for how to obtain and locate the DLL.

The macOS backend contains no AutoIt code and requires no AutoIt component. It
is an independent implementation, using Apple's Accessibility, Core Graphics,
and AppKit frameworks, of an API surface modeled on AutoItX's.
